    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it follows.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewritten. It no longer walks the repository for a per-city sequence (dropped entirely). It now builds `region + \"-\" + HASH8` where:\n- `REGION` = region derived from the postcode via the existing `OwnerLocality.of(city, postcode)` (postcode-preferred, city fallback, `UNKNOWN`).\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`, with the telephone put through `TelephoneE164.toE164` so it matches the stored E.164 form.\n\n**`OwnerLocality.forOwner`** \u2014 the locality derivation now reads the REGION segment out of the owner's `customerCode` (the new region-and-hash identity), falling back to postcode/city derivation for owners whose code isn't yet in that form (e.g. seed data). The value stays consistent with before, but it's now sourced from the identity.\n\nEverything else flows automatically from the new `customerCode`:\n- **Membership number** (`OwnerMapper`: `customerCode + \"-M\" + yy`) now yields e.g. `NSW-16E6609E-M26`.\n- **Check digit** (`Owner.getCheckDigit`, Luhn over the digits in `customerCode`) recomputes over the new digits.\n- **Create audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) logs the new code \u2014 the test run shows `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\nThe one dependency I removed was `AssignCustomerCode`'s `OwnerRepository` parameter, which was only used for the abandoned sequence count.\n\nTests: the acceptance test (`customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) and the full suite pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
